+or the bitwise OR of
+.Dv mtx_recursive
+and
+.Dv mtx_timed .
+.Fn mtx_lock
+blocks until the mutex is locked,
+.Fn mtx_trylock
+returns
+.Dv thrd_busy
+if the mutex is already locked,
+and
+.Fn mtx_timedlock
+blocks until the absolute
+.Fa ts
+time.
+.Pp
+.Fn cnd_init
+initializes a condition variable.
+.Fn cnd_wait
+and
+.Fn cnd_timedwait
+atomically release the mutex and wait for a signal;
+.Fn cnd_timedwait
+returns
+.Dv thrd_timedout
+when the absolute
+.Fa ts
+time passes.
+.Fn cnd_signal
+wakes one waiter and
+.Fn cnd_broadcast
+wakes all of them.
+.Pp
+.Fn tss_create
+creates a thread-specific storage key with destructor
+.Fa dtor ;
+.Fn tss_get
+and
+.Fn tss_set
+access the value associated with the calling thread.
+.Pp
+.Fn call_once
+calls
+.Fa func
+exactly once for a given
+.Fa flag .
+A
+.Vt once_flag
+must be initialized with
+.Dv ONCE_FLAG_INIT .
+.Pp
+The
+.Dv thread_local
+macro, available before ISO C23, is a synonym for
+.Va _Thread_local .
+.Sh RETURN VALUES
+The functions that can fail return
+.Dv thrd_success
+on success and one of
+.Dv thrd_timedout ,
+.Dv thrd_busy ,
+.Dv thrd_nomem
+or
+.Dv thrd_error
+on failure.
+.Pp
+Only
+.Fn thrd_create ,
+.Fn mtx_init
+and
+.Fn cnd_init
